{
  "title": "Iselin's Disease",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4073/iselins-disease",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 17 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Iselin's Disease is a common acquired condition cause by traction apophysitis of the the peroneus brevis tendon at the tuberosity of the fifth metatarsal in children and presents with lateral foot pain.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with pain over the 5th metartarsal base with radiographs showing an enlarged apophysis with disordered ossification and widened chondro-osseous junction.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually nonoperative with activity modifications, stretching, and a short period of cast immobilization as the condition typically resolves over time.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most often seen in physically active boys and girls between the ages of 8 and 13 years of age",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common in soccer players, basketball players, gymnasts, dancers, and other sports with repetitive inversion stresses",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "due to repetitive traction of peroneus brevis tendon at the site of its attachment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "fifth metatarsal apophysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Muscles",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "peroneus brevis tendon insertion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often no history of trauma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain in lateral foot",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "worse with activity and improves with rest",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "swelling and erythema",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tenderness over base of 5th metatarsal at the insertion of peroneus brevis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative test",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pain with resisted eversion and extreme plantar flexion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may show an enlarged apophysis with disordered ossification and widened chondro-osseous junction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4073/images/iselin_s.jpg",
                  "caption": "Radiographs skeletally immature patient demonstrating a longitudinally oriented apophysis with fragmentation consistent with Iselin&#39;s disease"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Normal apophysis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "longitudinally oriented apophysis without fragmentation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4073/images/normal_apophysis.jpg",
                  "caption": "Radiographs show a normal appearing fifth metatarsal apophysis. The apophysis is oriented in the long axis of the metatarsal with no fracture line through the apophysis."
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Base of 5th metatarsal fractures",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "transverse orientation of fracture fragment differentiates it from nearby vertically oriented apophysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4073/images/apophysis_and_fx_5th_mt.jpg",
                  "caption": "This oblique x-ray of the child&#39;s foot demonstrates the normal ossification of the fifth metatarsal apophysis where the peroneus brevis attaches (white arrow) which is more or less parallel to the long axis of the metatarsal. The black arrow demonstrates a proximal fifth metatarsal fracture, which tends to occur perpendicular to the long axis of the metatarsal. Courtesy Children&#39;s Orthopaedic Center, Los Angeles."
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may be difficult to differentiate in adolescents",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Os vesalianum",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "intratendinous accessory bone within the substance of the peroneus brevis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4073/images/os_vesalianum.jpg",
                  "caption": "Illustration showing the comparison of an os vesalianum versus Iselin&#39;s disease. Iselin&#39;s disease is seen as a fracture through the apophysis while an os vesalianum is an intraatendinous accessory bone in the substance of the peroneus brevis"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "often incidental but can be associated with pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "stretching, rest, activity modification, icing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "standard of care as conditions resolves with time",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cast immobilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "pain despite attempts at other non-surgical management",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "surgical excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "pain despite immobilization and other non-surgical management",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "nonunion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Nonunion**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rarely occurs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
